  "verbalization": "The compound (4S,4aR,7S,7aR,12bS)-9-ethoxy-3-methyl-2,4,4a,7,7a,13-hexahydro-1H-4,12-methanobenzofuro[3,2-e]isoquinolin-7-ol is associated with HUVEC through multiple pathways. It is identified as a target of Isopiline and Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP, which in turn targets HUVEC. Additionally, the compound is linked to 6,7-Dimethoxy-2-Methyl-3,4-Dihydroisoquinolin-1-One and 5-(2-Hydroxyacetyl)-10H-Phenazine-1-Carboxylic Acid, both of which also target HUVEC. These findings suggest that the compound may exert its effects on HUVEC through interactions with phosphatase enzymes, potentially modulating cellular signaling pathways. The evidence indicates a complex network of targets, with the compound acting as a central node in the interaction with HUVEC. The relationship is supported by multiple high-scoring pathways, but the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
